project.description:
The long-term goal of the project “Standardization of Modern Latvian Pronunciation” is to develop pronunciation norms and modern pronunciation dictionary of standard Latvian freely available for everyone that would represent the modern Latvian language. The objective of this interdisciplinary research project is to standardize Latvian pronunciation and develop fundamental phonetic resources.
The following tasks will be addressed in this project to achieve objective:
● to conduct acoustic phonetics research on current spelling issues, clarifying current pronunciation trends and submit recommendations to the Latvian Language Expert Commission;
● develop a research-based The Handbook of Modern Latvian Pronunciation;
● to develop The Latvian Phonetic Transcription Concept, defining the phonetic transcription principles,  phonetic characters and phonetic phenomena notation for traditional and IPA phonetic transcription;
● to develop a manually annotated phonetic dataset;
● to develop state-of-the-art Latvian phonetic transcription tool and evaluate its impact on speech synthesis;
● to extend the largest open Latvian online dictionary Tezaurs.lv with support for phonetic transcription and pronunciation sample curation.
